\nciteturn3view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.03031\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 168\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Cryptography and Security\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 6 Jan 2026 (【5†v1】), last revised 9 Jan 2026 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:FlexProofs: A Vector Commitment with Flexible Linear Time for Computing All Proofs\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Jing Liu】, 【7†Liang Feng Zhang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled FlexProofs: A Vector Commitment with Flexible Linear Time for Computing All Proofs, by Jing Liu and Liang Feng Zhang\nL14: \nL15: 【8†View PDF】 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:In this paper, we introduce FlexProofs, a new vector commitment (VC) scheme that achieves two key properties: (1) the prover can generate all individual opening proofs for a vector of size $N$ in optimal time ${\\cal O}(N)$, and there is a flexible batch size parameter $b$ that can be increased to further reduce the time to generate all proofs; and (2) the scheme is directly compatible with a family of zkSNARKs that encode their input as a multi-linear polynomial.\nL17: As a critical building block, we propose the first functional commitment (FC) scheme for multi-exponentiations with batch opening. Compared with HydraProofs, the only existing VC scheme that computes all proofs in optimal time ${\\cal O}(N)$ and is directly compatible with zkSNARKs, FlexProofs may speed up the process of generating all proofs, if the parameter $b$ is properly chosen. Our experiments show that for $N=2^{16}$ and $b=\\log^2 N$, FlexProofs can be $6\\times$ faster than HydraProofs.\nL18: Moreover, when combined with suitable zkSNARKs, FlexProofs enable practical applications such as verifiable secret sharing and verifiable robust aggregation.\nL19: Comments:  | Accepted by ACNS 2026\nL20: Subjects:  | Cryptography and Security (cs.CR); Logic in Computer Science (cs.LO)\nL21: Cite as:  | 【10†arXiv:2601.03031】 [cs.CR]\nL22:    | (or 【11†arXiv:2601.03031v2】 [cs.CR] for this version)\nL23:    | 【12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.03031†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Jing Liu [【13†view email】]\nL27: 【5†[v1]】 Tue, 6 Jan 2026 14:05:16 UTC (175 KB)\nL28: [v2] Fri, 9 Jan 2026 08:11:12 UTC (351 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled FlexProofs: A Vector Commitment with Flexible Linear Time for Computing All Proofs, by Jing Liu and Liang Feng Zhang\nL35: \nL36:   * 【8†View PDF】\nL37:   * 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL38:   * 【14†TeX Source】\nL39: \nL40: 【15†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL41: \nL42: ### Additional Features\nL43: \nL44:   * 【16†Audio Summary】\nL45: ### Current browse context:\nL46: \nL47: cs.CR\nL48: \nL49: 【17†< prev】   |   【18†next >】\nL50: \nL51: 【19†new】 | 【20†recent】 | 【21†2026-01】\nL52: \nL53: Change to browse by:\nL54: \nL55: 【22†cs】\nL56: 【23†cs.LO】\nL57: \nL58: ### References & Citations\nL59: \nL60:   * 【24†SciX†scixplorer.org】\nL61:   * 【25†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL62:   * 【26†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL63: \nL64: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL65: \nL66: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL67: \nL68: [Button: ×]\nL69: \nL70: loading...\nL71: \nL72: Data provided by:\nL73: \nL74: ### Bookmark\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL77: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL78: \nL79: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL80: \nL81: Bibliographic Explorer (【27†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL82: \nL83: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL84: \nL85: Connected Papers (【28†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com】)\nL86: \nL87: [Input] Litmaps 